"""Build a public evidence page from the current campaign application record."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json
from site_shell import apply_shell
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
d=json.loads((root/'docs/data/trump/reference-run.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
if d.get('schema_version')!=2:raise ValueError('Publish a campaign application record first.')
esc=html.escape;fmt=lambda n:f'{n:,}'
params=d['parameters']
topics=''.join(f'<tr><td>{t["id"]}</td><td>{esc(t.get("naming",{}).get("modal_label",", ".join(t["words"][:5])))}</td><td>{fmt(t["count"])}</td></tr>' for t in d['topics'])
status='The classifier has passed independent evaluation and actual human acceptance.' if d['classifier_validated'] else 'Campaign discovery is complete. Human theme synthesis and independent classifier validation must finish before presidential prevalence is reported.'
naming='The recorded run retains 500 completed naming votes per topic, including wording variation.' if d['naming_completed'] else 'Naming evidence is being collected for the adopted topics.'
body=f'''<p class="eyebrow">Campaign discovery → presidential measurement</p><h1>See the evidence.<br>Follow the decisions.</h1><p class="lede">One archive, two analytic roles. Discover a vocabulary of themes during the campaign, then evaluate how reliably those themes can be measured in presidential communication.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href="../app/">Explore the walkthrough →</a><a class="btn" href="../data/trump/campaign-evidence.zip">Download campaign evidence</a></div>
<div class="design-flow"><article><span>DISCOVER</span><strong>7,805</strong><p>Campaign posts<br>June 16, 2015–November 8, 2016</p></article><article><span>HUMAN REVIEW</span><strong>The codebook</strong><p>Interpret themes. Independently annotate. Evaluate and accept the classifier.</p></article><article><span>MEASURE</span><strong>26,239</strong><p>Presidential posts<br>January 20, 2017–January 8, 2021</p></article></div>
<h2>A reviewed starting point for interpretation.</h2><p>The search evaluated 1,200 candidate settings. The researcher selected a 12-topic candidate after inspecting original-post evidence. Its c<sub>v</sub> coherence is {params['coherence']:.4f}; the fitted model's assignments were verified after reconstruction and reload.</p><div class="tutorial-metrics"><div class="tutorial-metric"><strong>{len(d['topics'])}</strong><span>campaign topics adopted</span></div><div class="tutorial-metric"><strong>{fmt(d['discovery_records'])}</strong><span>campaign posts modeled</span></div><div class="tutorial-metric"><strong>{100*d['outliers']/d['discovery_records']:.1f}%</strong><span>modeled posts unassigned</span></div></div>
<div class="tutorial-table"><table><caption>Adopted campaign topics. Proposed names remain interpretation aids.</caption><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>{'Modal LLM name' if d['naming_completed'] else 'Representative words'}</th><th>Posts</th></tr></thead><tbody>{topics}</tbody></table></div><p>{naming} Researchers read those proposals alongside posts and relevant literature; model consistency is not independent expert agreement.</p>
<h2>Coverage matters as much as a score.</h2><p>Of the 7,805 campaign records, 7,779 retain modeled tokens and 26 are excluded from discovery after preprocessing. The adopted solution assigns 3,925 posts to topics and leaves 3,854 unassigned. Those unassigned posts remain part of the interpretive evidence. These discovery outcomes do not reduce the later presidential denominator.</p><p>The maximum-coherence solution placed 99.5% of its assigned posts in one broad cluster. The researcher selected a more differentiated candidate for interpretation. The numerical winner, every candidate and the explicit selection record remain preserved; the score was not silently substituted.</p>
<h2>Different stages establish different things.</h2><div class="tutorial-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Evidence</th><th>What it establishes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Campaign model and naming ballots</td><td>Computed groups and proposed descriptions of campaign language</td></tr><tr><td>Human synthesis</td><td>Researcher-defined meanings, boundaries and a frozen codebook</td></tr><tr><td>Development and held-out evaluation</td><td>Classifier selection followed by an independent assessment of its errors</td></tr><tr><td>Overall presidential prevalence</td><td>Shares of target posting events assigned to accepted themes, including the residual</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="tutorial-note">{status} Visitor drafts and small live experiments demonstrate operations; they do not supply research approval.</p>
<h2>Reproduce the process in your own environment.</h2><p>The repository connects each decision to a maintained Python script and a retained artifact. Reviewers interpret; agents execute the documented steps. The primary application estimates overall prevalence only, without period comparisons or causal claims. A fresh run may differ because probabilistic methods, model revisions and dependencies can change outputs.</p>
<details class="tutorial-note"><summary>Inspect the exact parameters and evidence</summary><div class="tutorial-table"><table><tbody><tr><th>Search</th><td>50 draws × ceilings 2–25; seed 42</td></tr><tr><th>Adopted draw / ceiling</th><td>{params['iteration']} / {params['max_topics']}</td></tr><tr><th>UMAP</th><td>{esc(json.dumps(params['umap_params']))}</td></tr><tr><th>HDBSCAN</th><td>{esc(json.dumps(params['hdbscan_params']))}</td></tr><tr><th>Embedding</th><td>all-MiniLM-L6-v2; pinned model revision in the run manifest</td></tr><tr><th>Discovery API calls</th><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href="../data/trump/reference-run.json">Application record</a> · <a href="../data/trump/campaign/all_iteration_results.json">Every candidate</a> · <a href="../data/trump/campaign/selection_record.json">Model choice</a> · <a href="../data/trump/campaign/assignments.csv">Assignments</a> · <a href="../data/trump/campaign/excluded.csv">Preprocessing exclusions</a> · <a href="../data/trump/campaign/run_manifest.json">Environment and hashes</a> · <a href="../data/trump/campaign/artifact-integrity.json">Artifact checksums</a></p><figure><img src="../data/trump/campaign/coherence_curve.png" alt="Coherence across topic ceilings for the adopted campaign parameter draw" style="width:100%;height:auto"><figcaption>The requested ceiling and the number of observed topics are different quantities.</figcaption></figure></details>
<div class="evidence-links"><a href="../reproduce/">Fork + run</a><a href="../paper/">Standalone methods</a><a href="../data/README.md">Data and attribution</a><a href="../audit/">Original research library</a></div>'''
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Campaign application evidence — TopicLLM</title><meta name="description" content="Inspect the campaign topics, researcher decisions and independent validation behind TopicLLM's presidential prevalence application."><link rel="stylesheet" href="../site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../reproduce.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../tutorial.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to evidence</a><main id="main" class="reproduce">{body}</main></body></html>'''
(root/'docs/validation/index.html').write_text(apply_shell(page),encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
print('Built the campaign evidence page from recorded artifacts.')
